  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Capture independent prechange exponent-overflow RED, add checked arithmetic for all dimension components, introduce typed absolute/interval temperature conversion and arithmetic, verify exact regressions, and complete C03 with durable boundary evidence.",
    "value": "Closes the dimensions and quantities capability with explicit integer-overflow behavior and tagged affine semantics, while preserving exact BigInteger values and legacy scalar unit APIs for compatibility.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Legacy scalar UnitDefinition.ToBase/FromBase remains backward compatible and cannot distinguish absolute from interval values; callers must select the tagged TemperatureMeasurement overload.",
      "Bare Quantity encodes physical dimensions but not temperature point/interval kind. Tagged TemperatureMeasurement is required at affine boundaries.",
      "Checked int exponents prevent silent wraparound but are not a general CPU/memory budget policy. No sibling repository integration is implied."
    ],
    "nextAction": "Refine and qualify M1-W01-C04 exact comparison and tolerance semantics, using its authorized source provenance and independent boundary oracles.",
